    "https://universityofmary.applytojob.com/apply/Yu7psMNnOO/Faculty-Mechanical-Engineering": {
      "title": "Thanks for visiting our Job Board. Please review our open positions and apply to the positions that match your qualifications.",
      "description": "Faculty | Mechanical Engineering - University of Mary - Career Page Skip To Job Description View All Jobs View Our Website Thanks for visiting our Job Board. Please review our open positions and apply to the positions that match your qualifications. Faculty | Mechanical Engineering Bismarck, ND Full Time Hamm School of Engineering Experienced Share Faculty / Mechanical Engineering The University of Mary invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Mechanical Engineering. This dynamic role includes teaching and developing engineering courses and laboratories, building strong industry relationships, serving on committees, and contributing to the ethical, moral, and leadership formation of students. The successful candidate will also integrate and synthesize within engineering courses the broad-based liberal arts knowledge and values that comprise the University's core curriculum for all students. All faculty are expected to demonstrate a willingness to support and advance the Christian, Catholic, and Benedictine mission and identity of the University of Mary (see www.umary.edu/about/mission/missionidentity.php ). Qualifications and Requirements Include: A Master’s degree or Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering is required A Ph.D. is preferred. The candidate should have the ability to create projects designed to enhance lectures, to guide and mentor students in engineering, to work closely with other faculty members, and to serve on committees in the University and the Community. The successful candidate will display enthusiasm for teaching and learning and is able to teach a wide variety of engineering courses and labs is preferred. Experience with Linux and C programming Knowledge and experience in LaTeX typesetting for scientific publications Upholds and supports the Christian, Catholic, Benedictine mission of the University of Mary Supports the ongoing implementation of Ex Corde Ecclesiae , the apostolic constitution on Catholic colleges and universities Builds a culture of ready and earnest hospitality in the Hamm School of Engineering and throughout the university, in accord with Saint Benedict’s admonition that all be received as Christ The University of Mary is a private, Christian, Catholic, Benedictine university that welcomes students of all faiths and backgrounds. Infusing Benedictine values throughout the educational experience, Mary offers distinguished, professionally-focused academic programs enlivened by the liberal arts, global and civic service, robust internships, and mentoring by respected faculty. As one of the most affordable private universities in the nation, Mary offers exceptional educational value as well as outstanding scholarship and financial aid opportunities. The University of Mary is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission of the North Central Association. For more information on the University of Mary, please watch a short video by clicking on this link: https://youtu.be/Go37Hy6QrVs How to Apply: Qualified applicants should submit (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) official or unofficial transcripts from all colleges and universities attended, and (4) three letters of recommendation. Additional attachments or anything larger than 5MB may be sent to [email protected] . Equal Opportunity Employer Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file What's your citizenship / employment eligibility? * No answer I am a U.S. Citizen/Permanent Resident Non-citizen allowed to work for any employer Non-citizen allowed to work for current employer Non-citizen seeking work authorization I am a Canadian Citizen/Permanent Resident Other Please upload your cover letter Please provide official or unof